<title>AUSTRALIA: AURORA LIFTS INDONESIA SITE GOLD RESERVES.</title>
<headline>AURORA LIFTS INDONESIA SITE GOLD RESERVES.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aurora Gold Ltd said on Thursday it had increased gold and silver reserves at its Toka Tindung project in north Sualwesi, Indonesia, by about 50 percent to 612,000 gold equivalent ounces.</p>
<p>Total estimated proven and probable ore reserves are now 4.74 million tonnes grading 3.9 grams per tonne (g/t) gold and 11 g/t silver, Aurora said.</p>
<p>A decision over whether to develop the prospect will be made following the completion of a feasibility study at the end of September, Aurora said.</p>
<p>-- James Regan, Perth Bureau 61-8 9221-7111</p>
